(CLI-08: `-v`, `--verbose` - verbose output. Both spellings hand-verified
 to print the identical five-line pipeline log to stdout during
 compilation; that log is a compile-time side effect, not something the
 RUN of the resulting binary shows, so check-probes.sh's standard
 compile-then-run below can only confirm the flag doesn't change runtime
 behavior - the verbose transcript itself is hand-verified separately.
 Hand-run separately (both spellings, byte-identical output):
   $ vox hello.vox -v -o hello_v
   Compiling hello.vox...
   Generated hello.asm
   Assembling...
   Linking...
   Created executable: hello_v
   Removed assembly file: hello.asm
   $ vox hello.vox --verbose -o hello_verbose
   Compiling hello.vox...
   Generated hello.asm
   Assembling...
   Linking...
   Created executable: hello_verbose
   Removed assembly file: hello.asm
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox CLI-08.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Hello, World!
)
Print "Hello, World!".
